    <!-- The page that explains it -->
    <string name="absorbed_title">Estimated absorbed</string>
    <string name="absorbed_intro">The mg on a pack is the nicotine each piece or spray holds, or a patch releases. Not all of it reaches your blood. Some is swallowed and broken down first, and some stays in the gum or the cartridge.</string>
    <string name="absorbed_switch">Show estimated absorbed amounts</string>
    <string name="absorbed_switch_detail">Beside the labelled mg on Today, in History and on the log sheet</string>
    <string name="absorbed_how_heading">How it\'s worked out</string>
    <string name="absorbed_how">Each kind of product has one rough share, from product leaflets and published studies. A 4\u00A0mg piece of gum shows as about 2\u00A0mg absorbed.</string>
    <string name="absorbed_varies">These are rough averages. How much you absorb depends on how you chew, suck, spray or puff, and it varies a lot from person to person.</string>
    <string name="absorbed_labelled">Your plan, its guide and allowances, weekly results, achievements and Insights always use the labelled mg.</string>
    <string name="absorbed_not_advice">This isn\'t medical advice. A pharmacist can tell you more about the products you use.</string>
